<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. wheat major net sales activity in the week ended Aug 29 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:    1996/97		   1997/98</p>
<p> Egypt	  210,000		    Nil</p>
<p> Taiwan	  97,200</p>
<p> China	   82,000-A</p>
<p> South Africa  56,700</p>
<p> Unknown     -161,100</p>
<p> Brazil	 -57,600-B</p>
<p>A- includes 65,000 tonnes changed from unknown. B- cancellations.</p>
<p>Net sales of 432,300 tonnes were 27 percent below the previous week and seven percent lower than the four-week average.</p>
<p>Exports of 743,600 tonnes were 16 percent lower than the prior week and 11 percent less than the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary Export Destinations: Pakistan, the Philippines, Japan, China, Peru, Indonesia and Egypt.</p>
</text>
